{
  "Dockerfile": "- **File Path**: `Dockerfile`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides instructions for building a Docker image for the Go SSE chat application using a multi-stage build process to create a small, efficient, and production-ready image.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Instructions / Commands**:\n        - `FROM golang:1.21-alpine AS builder`: (Stage 1: Builder) Uses a Go 1.21 Alpine image for compiling the application.\n        - `WORKDIR /app`: Sets the working directory inside the container.\n        - `COPY go.mod go.sum ./`: Copies Go module definition files to leverage Docker's layer caching for dependencies.\n        - `RUN go mod download`: Downloads Go module dependencies.\n        - `COPY . .`: Copies the entire source code into the builder stage.\n        - `RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux go build -ldflags=\"-w -s\" -o /server ./cmd/server`: Compiles the Go application into a static binary named `server`, optimized for Linux and stripped of debug info.\n        - `FROM alpine:latest`: (Stage 2: Final) Uses a minimal Alpine Linux image as the base for the final image.\n        - `WORKDIR /app`: Sets the working directory for the final image.\n        - `COPY --from=builder /server .`: Copies only the compiled `server` binary from the builder stage to the final image.\n        - `COPY configs/config.yaml ./configs/`: Copies the application's configuration file.\n        - `EXPOSE 8080`: Informs Docker that the container listens on port 8080 at runtime.\n        - `CMD [\"./server\"]`: Specifies the command to run when the container starts, executing the compiled application.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Multi-Stage Build**: Significantly reduces the final image size by separating the build environment (Go compiler, tools) from the runtime environment (just the compiled binary and config).\n    - **Dependency Caching**: Optimizes build times by copying `go.mod` and `go.sum` first, allowing Docker to cache dependency downloads.\n    - **Static Compilation**: `CGO_ENABLED=0` ensures the Go binary is statically linked, making it highly portable and suitable for minimal base images like Alpine.\n    - **Minimal Base Image**: Uses `alpine:latest` for the final image, resulting in a very small attack surface and faster downloads.\n",
  "Makefile": "- **File Path**: `Makefile`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides a set of convenient commands (targets) for common development and deployment tasks related to the Go SSE chat application, including local execution, binary building, and Docker container management.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `BINARY_NAME`: `server` (The name of the compiled Go binary).\n        - `BINARY_PATH`: `./bin/$(BINARY_NAME)` (The target path for the compiled binary).\n    - **Functions / Methods**: (Represented by Makefile targets)\n        - `run`: (Public target) Executes the Go application directly using `go run ./cmd/server/main.go`.\n        - `build`: (Public target) Compiles the Go application into an executable binary for the local operating system, placing it in the `./bin/` directory.\n        - `docker-build`: (Public target) Builds the Docker image for the application using the `Dockerfile` in the current directory and tags it as `sse-chat-app`.\n        - `docker-up`: (Public target) Starts the application and its dependencies (Redis) using `docker-compose up -d`, running them in detached mode.\n        - `docker-down`: (Public target) Stops and removes the Docker containers, networks, and volumes defined in `docker-compose.yaml`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Task Automation**: Simplifies complex commands into easy-to-remember targets.\n    - **`.PHONY` Targets**: Declares targets as phony to ensure they are always executed, even if a file with the same name exists.\n    - **Variable Usage**: Uses variables (`BINARY_NAME`, `BINARY_PATH`) for better maintainability and consistency.",
  "cmd/server/main.go": "- **File Path**: `cmd/server/main.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: The main entry point for the SSE chat application. It handles application startup, configuration loading, Redis client initialization, dependency injection for repositories and use cases, HTTP server setup, a background task for inactive user cleanup, and graceful shutdown.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `main()`: (Public) The application's entry point.\n            - Loads configuration from `configs/config.yaml` and overrides with environment variables (`SERVER_PORT`, `REDIS_ADDR`).\n            - Initializes and pings a Redis client.\n            - Creates instances of `RedisUserRepository` and `RedisEventRepository`.\n            - Creates instances of `UserUsecase` and `EventUsecase`, injecting their respective repository dependencies.\n            - Starts a background goroutine that periodically calls `userUsecase.CleanupInactiveUsers` to remove old user data. This routine respects the main application context for shutdown.\n            - Initializes the main HTTP handler and router using `transportHTTP.NewHandler` and `InitRoutes`.\n            - Starts the HTTP server in a goroutine.\n            - Implements graceful shutdown by listening for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` signals, allowing the server to shut down cleanly within a timeout.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Application Entry Point**: Orchestrates the entire application lifecycle.\n    - **Configuration Management**: Loads settings from a YAML file and supports environment variable overrides.\n    - **Dependency Injection**: Manually constructs and injects dependencies (Redis client, repositories, use cases) into higher-level components.\n    - **Background Processing**: Runs a periodic task (inactive user cleanup) concurrently using a goroutine and `time.Ticker`.\n    - **Graceful Shutdown**: Implements a robust mechanism to shut down the HTTP server and background tasks upon receiving termination signals.\n",
  "configs/config.yaml": "- **File Path**: `configs/config.yaml`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Configuration file for the application, specifying server port, Redis connection details, and application-specific timeouts.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `server.port`: (String) The network address and port for the HTTP server (e.g., \":8080\").\n        - `redis.addr`: (String) The address of the Redis server (e.g., \"localhost:6379\").\n        - `redis.password`: (String) The password for Redis authentication (can be empty).\n        - `redis.db`: (Integer) The Redis database number to use.\n        - `app.user_inactive_timeout_minutes`: (Integer) The duration in minutes after which a user is considered inactive.\n        - `app.username_cooldown_minutes`: (Integer) The duration in minutes for which a username is on cooldown after being released.\n",
  "docker-compose.yaml": "- **File Path**: `docker-compose.yaml`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines and orchestrates the multi-container environment for the SSE chat application, including a Redis service and the Go application service. It specifies how these services are built, configured, and linked.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `version`: `3.8` (Docker Compose file format version).\n        - `services.redis`:\n            - `image`: `redis:alpine` (Uses the official Redis Alpine image).\n            - `ports`: `6379:6379` (Maps container port 6379 to host port 6379).\n            - `volumes`: `redis_data:/data` (Mounts a named volume for Redis data persistence).\n            - `restart`: `unless-stopped` (Restarts the container unless explicitly stopped).\n        - `services.app`:\n            - `build`: `.` (Builds the Docker image from the current directory using the `Dockerfile`).\n            - `ports`: `8080:8080` (Maps container port 8080 to host port 8080).\n            - `depends_on`: `redis` (Ensures the Redis service starts before the app service).\n            - `environment`:\n                - `REDIS_ADDR=redis:6379` (Overrides the Redis address in the app's configuration to point to the Redis service within the Docker network).\n                - `SERVER_PORT=:8080` (Overrides the server port).\n            - `restart`: `unless-stopped` (Restarts the container unless explicitly stopped).\n        - `volumes.redis_data`: (Named volume for Redis data persistence).\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Multi-service Orchestration**: Defines and manages multiple interdependent services (application and database).\n    - **Environment Variable Overrides**: Demonstrates how to override application configuration settings using environment variables for containerized deployments.\n    - **Data Persistence**: Uses a named volume to ensure Redis data persists across container restarts.\n    - **Service Dependency**: Specifies that the application service depends on the Redis service.\n",
  "go.mod": "- **File Path**: `go.mod`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the Go module path and lists all direct and indirect external dependencies required by the `sse-chat` project, along with the Go version.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `module`: `sse-chat` (Module path)\n        - `go`: `1.21` (Required Go version)\n        - `require`: (List of direct dependencies)\n            - `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.0.12`\n            - `github.com/go-redis/redis/v8 v8.11.5`\n            - `github.com/google/uuid v1.6.0`\n            - `gopkg.in/yaml.v2 v2.4.0`\n        - `require` (indirect): (List of indirect dependencies)\n            - `github.com/cespare/xxhash/v2 v2.1.2`\n            - `github.com/dgryski/go-rendezvous v0.0.0-20200823014737-9f7001d12a5f`\n            - `github.com/onsi/ginkgo v1.16.5`\n            - `github.com/onsi/gomega v1.17.0`\n",
  "internal/config/config.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/config/config.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the application's configuration structure and provides a utility function to load these settings from a YAML file.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `Config`: (Public struct) The top-level configuration structure for the application.\n            - Nested Struct `Server`:\n                - Fields: `Port` (string, YAML tag `port`).\n            - Nested Struct `Redis`:\n                - Fields: `Addr` (string, YAML tag `addr`), `Password` (string, YAML tag `password`), `DB` (int, YAML tag `db`).\n            - Nested Struct `App`:\n                - Fields: `UserInactiveTimeout` (time.Duration, YAML tag `user_inactive_timeout_minutes`), `UsernameCooldown` (time.Duration, YAML tag `username_cooldown_minutes`).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `LoadConfig(path string) (*Config, error)`: (Public) Reads a YAML file from the given path, unmarshals its content into a `Config` struct, and converts the `user_inactive_timeout_minutes` and `username_cooldown_minutes` fields from integer minutes to `time.Duration`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Configuration management using YAML.\n    - Custom unmarshaling logic for `time.Duration` from integer minutes.",
  "internal/domain/event.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/domain/event.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the `Event` data structure and various `EventType` constants, which are used to represent different occurrences or messages within the chat system, likely for Server-Sent Events (SSE).\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `EventType`: (Public type) A string alias used to categorize different types of events.\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `UserJoined`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user joining event.\n        - `UserLeft`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user leaving event.\n        - `UsernameChanged`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a username change event.\n        - `Message`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a chat message event.\n        - `TypingStart`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user starting to type event.\n        - `TypingStop`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user stopping typing event.\n        - `Heartbeat`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a heartbeat event.\n        - `Event`: (Public struct) Represents a generic event in the system.\n            - Fields: `EventID` (string), `Timestamp` (time.Time), `Type` (EventType), `FromUserID` (string, optional), `ToUserID` (string, optional), `Payload` (map[string]interface{}).\n",
  "internal/domain/user.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/domain/user.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the `User` data structure, representing the core user entity within the application's domain.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `User`: (Public struct) Represents a user in the chat system.\n            - Fields: `UserID` (string, JSON tag `userId`), `Username` (string, JSON tag `username`), `LastActive` (time.Time, JSON ignored), `IsOnline` (bool, JSON tag `isOnline`), `LastDeliveredEventID` (string, JSON ignored).\n",
  "internal/repository/redis_event_repository.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/repository/redis_event_repository.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Implements the `EventRepository` interface, providing data access operations for `Event` entities using Redis. It leverages Redis Streams for user-specific event logs and Redis Pub/Sub for global event broadcasts.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `redisEventRepository`: (Private struct) Implements the `usecase.EventRepository` interface.\n            - Fields: `client` (*redis.Client).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewRedisEventRepository(client *redis.Client) usecase.EventRepository`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `redisEventRepository` instance.\n        - `userStreamKey(userID string) string`: (Private) Generates a Redis key string for a specific user's event stream.\n        - `(r *redisEventRepository) PublishEventToUser(ctx context.Context, userID string, event *domain.Event) error`: (Public method) Adds an event to a user's dedicated Redis Stream using `XADD`. It also sets the `EventID` on the provided `domain.Event` object.\n        - `(r *redisEventRepository) PublishEventToAll(ctx context.Context, event *domain.Event) error`: (Public method) Publishes an event to a global Redis Pub/Sub channel, broadcasting it to all subscribers.\n        - `(r *redisEventRepository) GetEventsForUserAfter(ctx context.Context, userID, lastEventID string) ([]*domain.Event, error)`: (Public method) Retrieves a range of events from a user's Redis Stream using `XRANGE`, starting after a specified `lastEventID`.\n        - `(r *redisEventRepository) GetEventsForUserBlocking(ctx context.Context, userID, lastEventID string, timeout time.Duration) ([]*domain.Event, error)`: (Public method) Retrieves events from a user's Redis Stream using `XREAD`, blocking for a specified `timeout` until new events are available or the timeout expires.\n        - `(r *redisEventRepository) SubscribeToBroadcasts(ctx context.Context) *redis.PubSub`: (Public method) Subscribes to the global broadcast channel using Redis Pub/Sub, returning a `*redis.PubSub` client.\n        - `eventToMap(event *domain.Event) (map[string]interface{}, error)`: (Private) Helper function to convert a `domain.Event` struct into a map suitable for storage in a Redis Stream entry.\n        - `mapToEvent(eventID string, data map[string]interface{}) (*domain.Event, error)`: (Private) Helper function to convert a map retrieved from a Redis Stream entry back into a `domain.Event` struct.\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `broadcastChannel`: (Private, string) The name of the Redis Pub/Sub channel used for global event broadcasts.\n        - `maxStreamLen`: (Private, int) The maximum approximate length of a Redis Stream for user events, used to cap stream size.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Repository Pattern**: Abstracts the data access logic for event entities.\n    - **Redis Streams**: Utilizes Redis Streams (`XADD`, `XRANGE`, `XREAD`) for persistent, ordered, and user-specific event logs, which is crucial for Server-Sent Events (SSE).\n    - **Redis Pub/Sub**: Employs Redis Pub/Sub for broadcasting events to all connected application instances.\n    - **Data Serialization**: Marshals and unmarshals `domain.Event` payloads to/from JSON strings when interacting with Redis.\n",
  "internal/repository/redis_user_repository.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/repository/redis_user_repository.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Implements the `UserRepository` interface, providing concrete data access operations for `User` entities using Redis as the persistence layer. It manages user profiles, active user lists, and username availability/cooldowns.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `redisUserRepository`: (Private struct) Implements the `usecase.UserRepository` interface.\n            - Fields: `client` (*redis.Client).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `userKey(userID string) string`: (Private) Generates a Redis key string for a specific user's data.\n        - `usernameCooldownKey(username string) string`: (Private) Generates a Redis key string for a username's cooldown status.\n        - `NewRedisUserRepository(client *redis.Client) *redisUserRepository`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `redisUserRepository` instance.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) Create(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: (Public method) Creates a new user in Redis by storing their details in a hash, adding them to a sorted set of active users, and adding their username to a set of taken usernames. Uses a Redis transaction pipeline.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) FindByID(ctx context.Context, userID string) (*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Retrieves a user's details from Redis based on their `UserID`.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) Update(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: (Public method) Updates an existing user's details in Redis, including their activity timestamp and username. Uses a Redis transaction pipeline.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) Delete(ctx context.Context, userID string) error`: (Public method) Deletes a user's data from Redis, removing their hash, active user entry, and username. Uses a Redis transaction pipeline.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) GetActiveUsers(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Fetches all active users from Redis, retrieving their full details.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) FindInactiveUsers(ctx context.Context, timeout time.Duration) ([]string, error)`: (Public method) Queries Redis to find IDs of users whose last active timestamp is older than the specified timeout.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) IsUsernameTaken(ctx context.Context, username string) (bool, error)`: (Public method) Checks if a given username is currently registered in the system.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) ReleaseUsername(ctx context.Context, username string, cooldown time.Duration) error`: (Public method) Removes a username from the set of taken usernames and places it on a temporary cooldown. Uses a Redis transaction pipeline.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) IsUsernameOnCooldown(ctx context.Context, username string) (bool, error)`: (Public method) Checks if a specific username is currently in a cooldown period.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) UpdateLastDeliveredEventID(ctx context.Context, userID, eventID string) error`: (Public method) Updates the `lastDeliveredEventId` field for a user in Redis.\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `activeUsersKey`: (Private, string) Redis key for the sorted set storing active user IDs and their last active timestamps.\n        - `usernamesKey`: (Private, string) Redis key for the set storing all currently taken usernames.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Repository Pattern**: Abstracts the data access logic for user entities.\n    - **Redis Data Structures**: Leverages Redis Hashes for individual user data, Sorted Sets for tracking active users by their last activity, and Sets for managing unique usernames.\n    - **Redis Transactions**: Uses `redis.TxPipeline` to ensure atomicity for operations involving multiple Redis commands (e.g., `Create`, `Update`, `Delete`, `ReleaseUsername`).\n",
  "internal/transport/http/event_handler.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/event_handler.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Handles HTTP requests related to chat events, such as sending messages, broadcasting typing status, and providing an initial snapshot of events and active users. It acts as a bridge between HTTP requests and the `EventUsecase` business logic.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `EventHandler`: (Public struct) Holds the `usecase.EventUsecase` dependency.\n            - Fields: `uc` (usecase.EventUsecase).\n        - `sendMessageRequest`: (Private struct) Data Transfer Object (DTO) for the request body when sending a message.\n            - Fields: `FromUserID` (string), `ToUserID` (string), `Text` (string).\n        - `sendTypingRequest`: (Private struct) DTO for the request body when sending a typing status.\n            - Fields: `UserID` (string), `ToUserID` (string), `Typing` (bool).\n        - `snapshotResponse`: (Private struct) DTO for the response body when requesting a snapshot.\n            - Fields: `Events` ([]*domain.Event), `ActiveUsers` ([]*domain.User).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewEventHandler(uc usecase.EventUsecase) *EventHandler`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `EventHandler` instance.\n        - `(h *EventHandler) SendMessage(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) Handles HTTP POST requests to `/api/message`. It decodes the request body, calls `EventUsecase.SendMessage`, and responds with `HTTP 202 Accepted` or an appropriate error status.\n        - `(h *EventHandler) SendTypingStatus(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) Handles HTTP POST requests to `/api/typing`. It decodes the request body, calls `EventUsecase.BroadcastTyping`, and responds with `HTTP 202 Accepted` or an error.\n        - `(h *EventHandler) GetSnapshot(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) Handles HTTP GET requests to `/api/snapshot`. It extracts `userId` and `lastEventId` from query parameters, calls `EventUsecase.GetSnapshot`, and responds with a JSON object containing events and active users.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **HTTP Handler Pattern**: Responsible for parsing HTTP requests, invoking business logic, and formatting HTTP responses.\n    - **Data Transfer Objects (DTOs)**: Uses specific structs (`sendMessageRequest`, `sendTypingRequest`, `snapshotResponse`) for request and response serialization/deserialization.\n    - **Error Handling**: Maps usecase-specific errors (e.g., `ErrMessageTooLong`) to appropriate HTTP status codes.\n",
  "internal/transport/http/handler.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/handler.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Configures and initializes the main HTTP router for the application, applying global and endpoint-specific middleware, and mapping API routes to their respective handlers. It also serves static frontend files.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `Handler`: (Public struct) Holds the necessary use case and repository dependencies for the HTTP handlers.\n            - Fields: `userUsecase` (usecase.UserUsecase), `eventUsecase` (usecase.EventUsecase), `eventRepo` (usecase.EventRepository), `redisClient` (*redis.Client).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewHandler(userUsecase usecase.UserUsecase, eventUsecase usecase.EventUsecase, eventRepo usecase.EventRepository, redisClient *redis.Client) *Handler`: (Public) Constructor function for `Handler`.\n        - `(h *Handler) InitRoutes() *chi.Mux`: (Public method) Initializes and returns a `chi.Mux` router.\n            - Applies global middleware: `middleware.RequestID`, `middleware.RealIP`, custom `mw.Logger`, `middleware.Recoverer`, and `middleware.Heartbeat` (on `/ping`).\n            - Defines an `/api` route group.\n            - Within the `/api` group, it creates `UserHandler`, `EventHandler`, and `SSEHandler` instances.\n            - Applies specific `mw.RateLimiter` middleware to `/api/join` (3 requests/min), `/api/change-username` (1 request/30s), and `/api/message` (5 requests/5s) endpoints.\n            - Maps HTTP POST requests for user actions (`/join`, `/change-username`), event actions (`/message`, `/typing`), and GET requests for event snapshots (`/snapshot`) and SSE streams (`/sse`) to their respective handler methods.\n            - Configures serving of static files from the `./public` directory for all other routes.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **HTTP Router**: Uses `github.com/go-chi/chi` for declarative and group-based routing.\n    - **Middleware Chain**: Organizes a sequence of middleware functions (both standard and custom) to apply cross-cutting concerns like logging, request ID generation, and rate limiting.\n    - **Endpoint-Specific Middleware**: Demonstrates applying different rate limiting rules to individual API endpoints using `chi.Router` groups.\n    - **Static File Serving**: Provides a mechanism to serve static assets (e.g., HTML, CSS, JavaScript) for the frontend.",
  "internal/transport/http/middleware/logger.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/middleware/logger.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines an HTTP middleware function responsible for logging details of incoming requests and their responses.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `Logger(next http.Handler) http.Handler`: (Public) A middleware function that wraps an `http.Handler`. It captures and logs information about each HTTP request, including the method, path, remote address, HTTP status code, request latency, and a unique request ID, using structured logging (`slog`).\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **HTTP Middleware**: Implements the standard Go `http.Handler` middleware pattern to intercept and process requests.\n    - **Structured Logging**: Utilizes `log/slog` for consistent and machine-readable logging of request lifecycle events.\n",
  "internal/transport/http/middleware/ratelimiter.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/middleware/ratelimiter.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides an HTTP middleware for rate limiting requests based on the client's IP address, using Redis to track request counts within a defined time window.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `RateLimiter(client *redis.Client, keyPrefix string, limit int, window time.Duration) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: (Public) A higher-order function that returns an HTTP middleware. This middleware tracks the number of requests from a client (identified by `r.RemoteAddr`) using Redis's `INCR` command and sets an `EXPIRE` on the key. If the request count exceeds the `limit` within the `window`, it responds with `HTTP 429 Too Many Requests`. It also adds `X-RateLimit-Limit` and `X-RateLimit-Remaining` headers to the response.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **HTTP Middleware**: Implements the standard Go `http.Handler` middleware pattern.\n    - **Rate Limiting**: Implements a basic sliding window counter rate limiting strategy using Redis.\n    - **Redis Transactions/Pipelines**: Uses a Redis pipeline to atomically increment the counter and set/reset the expiration for the rate limit key, reducing round-trip latency.\n",
  "internal/transport/http/sse_handler.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/sse_handler.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Implements the Server-Sent Events (SSE) endpoint, enabling clients to receive real-time event updates. It manages the SSE connection lifecycle, including initial event catch-up, continuous event streaming, and sending heartbeats.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `SSEHandler`: (Public struct) Holds dependencies for `UserUsecase` and `EventRepository`.\n            - Fields: `userUsecase` (usecase.UserUsecase), `eventRepo` (usecase.EventRepository).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewSSEHandler(userUC usecase.UserUsecase, eventRepo usecase.EventRepository) *SSEHandler`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `SSEHandler` instance.\n        - `(h *SSEHandler) ServeHTTP(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) The main HTTP handler for the `/api/sse` endpoint. It sets up SSE headers, performs an initial catch-up of events missed by the client, starts a heartbeat ticker, and enters a continuous loop to fetch and send new events from the user's Redis stream, blocking until new events are available or a timeout occurs. It handles context cancellation for graceful stream closure.\n        - `(h *SSEHandler) sendEvents(ctx context.Context, w http.ResponseWriter, flusher http.Flusher, userID string, events []*domain.Event, lastEventID string) string`: (Private method) Iterates through a slice of events, sends each one to the client, and updates the user's `lastDeliveredEventID` in the database.\n        - `(h *SSEHandler) sendHeartbeat(w http.ResponseWriter, flusher http.Flusher) error`: (Private method) Sends a `domain.Heartbeat` event to the client to keep the connection alive.\n        - `(h *SSEHandler) sendEvent(w http.ResponseWriter, flusher http.Flusher, event *domain.Event) error`: (Private method) Formats a `domain.Event` into the SSE message format (id, event type, data) and sends it to the client.\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `heartbeatInterval`: (Private, time.Duration) The duration between sending heartbeat events to the client.\n        - `redisBlockTimeout`: (Private, time.Duration) The maximum time to block on Redis for new events before checking for context cancellation or sending a heartbeat.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Server-Sent Events (SSE)**: Implements the SSE protocol for real-time, unidirectional communication from server to client.\n    - **Long Polling / Blocking Reads**: Uses `EventRepository.GetEventsForUserBlocking` to efficiently wait for new events from Redis Streams, minimizing CPU usage.\n    - **Heartbeats**: Sends periodic heartbeat messages to prevent connection timeouts and detect unresponsive clients.\n    - **Event Catch-up**: Retrieves and sends any events that occurred while the client was disconnected, using the `Last-Event-ID` header.\n    - **Context Cancellation**: Integrates `context.Context` to gracefully shut down the SSE stream when the client disconnects or the server is shutting down.\n",
  "internal/transport/http/user_handler.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/user_handler.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Handles specific HTTP requests related to user operations (joining the chat, changing username) by interacting with the `UserUsecase` layer.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `UserHandler`: (Public struct) Holds the `usecase.UserUsecase` dependency.\n        - `joinRequest`: (Private struct) Data Transfer Object (DTO) for the request body of the `/join` endpoint.\n            - Fields: `DesiredUsername` (string).\n        - `joinResponse`: (Private struct) DTO for the response body of the `/join` endpoint.\n            - Fields: `UserID` (string), `Username` (string), `ActiveUsers` (interface{}).\n        - `changeUsernameRequest`: (Private struct) DTO for the request body of the `/change-username` endpoint.\n            - Fields: `UserID` (string), `NewUsername` (string).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewUserHandler(uc usecase.UserUsecase) *UserHandler`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `UserHandler` instance.\n        - `(h *UserHandler) Join(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) Handles HTTP POST requests to `/api/join`. It decodes the request, calls the `UserUsecase.Join` method, and responds with the new user's details and active users, or an appropriate HTTP error status.\n        - `(h *UserHandler) ChangeUsername(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) Handles HTTP POST requests to `/api/change-username`. It decodes the request, calls the `UserUsecase.ChangeUsername` method, and responds with a success status or an appropriate HTTP error status based on the usecase's error.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - HTTP Handler pattern, responsible for request/response handling and delegating to the usecase layer.\n    - Uses DTOs for request and response bodies.\n    - Specific error handling and HTTP status code mapping for usecase errors.\n",
  "internal/usecase/event_usecase.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/usecase/event_usecase.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Implements the `EventUsecase` interface, providing the business logic for managing chat events such as sending messages, broadcasting typing status, and retrieving event snapshots. It orchestrates interactions between the `EventRepository` and `UserRepository`.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `eventUsecase`: (Private struct) Implements the `usecase.EventUsecase` interface.\n            - Fields: `eventRepo` (EventRepository), `userRepo` (UserRepository).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewEventUsecase(eventRepo EventRepository, userRepo UserRepository) EventUsecase`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `eventUsecase` instance.\n        - `(uc *eventUsecase) SendMessage(ctx context.Context, fromUserID, toUserID, text string) (*domain.Event, error)`: (Public method) Handles the logic for sending a chat message. It validates the message length, creates a `domain.Message` event, publishes it to both the sender's and recipient's event streams, and updates the sender's last active timestamp.\n        - `(uc *eventUsecase) BroadcastTyping(ctx context.Context, fromUserID, toUserID string, isTyping bool) error`: (Public method) Handles the logic for broadcasting a user's typing status. It creates a `domain.TypingStart` or `domain.TypingStop` event, publishes it to the recipient's event stream, and updates the sender's last active timestamp.\n        - `(uc *eventUsecase) GetSnapshot(ctx context.Context, userID, lastEventID string) ([]*domain.Event, []*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Retrieves a snapshot of events for a specific user (events after `lastEventID`) and a list of all currently active users.\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `ErrMessageTooLong`: (Public, error) An error indicating that a message's text exceeds the maximum allowed length.\n        - `maxMessageLength`: (Private, int) The maximum number of characters allowed for a chat message.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Usecase Pattern**: Encapsulates the core business rules for event management, acting as an intermediary between HTTP handlers and repositories.\n    - **Event-Driven Logic**: Creates and processes `domain.Event` objects to represent various chat occurrences.\n    - **Input Validation**: Performs checks on message content (e.g., length, emptiness).\n    - **Activity Tracking**: Automatically updates the sender's `LastActive` timestamp when they send a message or typing status.\n",
  "internal/usecase/interfaces.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/usecase/interfaces.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the interfaces for the application's use case and repository layers, establishing clear contracts for business logic and data access operations related to users and events.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `UserRepository`: (Public interface) Defines methods for CRUD operations on `domain.User` entities, managing active users, checking username availability/cooldown, and updating event delivery status.\n        - `UserUsecase`: (Public interface) Defines methods for user-related business logic, including joining, changing username, updating activity, disconnecting, and cleaning up inactive users.\n        - `EventRepository`: (Public interface) Defines methods for persisting and retrieving `domain.Event` objects, including publishing to user-specific streams, broadcasting globally, and subscribing to broadcast channels.\n        - `EventUsecase`: (Public interface) Defines methods for event-related business logic, such as sending messages, broadcasting typing status, and retrieving a snapshot of events and active users.\n",
  "internal/usecase/user_usecase.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/usecase/user_usecase.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Implements the `UserUsecase` interface, providing the business logic for user management within the chat application. This includes operations like user registration (joining), username changes, activity tracking, disconnections, and periodic cleanup of inactive users.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `userUsecase`: (Private struct) Implements the `usecase.UserUsecase` interface.\n            - Fields: `userRepo` (UserRepository), `userInactiveTimeout` (time.Duration), `usernameCooldown` (time.Duration).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewUserUsecase(userRepo UserRepository, inactiveTimeout, cooldown time.Duration) UserUsecase`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `userUsecase` instance.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) Join(ctx context.Context, desiredUsername string) (*domain.User, []*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Handles the logic for a user joining the chat. It validates the username, checks for availability (and modifies if taken), creates the user via the repository, and returns the new user along with a list of active users.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) ChangeUsername(ctx context.Context, userID, newUsername string) (string, error)`: (Public method) Handles the logic for a user changing their username. It validates the new username, checks for availability and cooldown status, updates the user's profile, and places the old username on cooldown.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) UpdateActivity(ctx context.Context, userID string) error`: (Public method) Updates a user's `LastActive` timestamp, marking them as recently active.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) Disconnect(ctx context.Context, userID string) (*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Marks a user as offline (`IsOnline = false`) in the repository.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) CleanupInactiveUsers(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Identifies users who have been inactive for longer than `userInactiveTimeout`, deletes their profiles, and releases their usernames to cooldown.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) UpdateLastDeliveredEventID(ctx context.Context, userID, eventID string) error`: (Public method) Delegates to the `UserRepository` to update the last event ID successfully delivered to a user.\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `ErrUsernameTaken`: (Public, error) An error indicating that the desired username is already in use.\n        - `ErrUsernameOnCooldown`: (Public, error) An error indicating that the desired username is temporarily unavailable due to a cooldown period.\n        - `ErrUserNotFound`: (Public, error) An error indicating that a user could not be found.\n        - `ErrInvalidUsername`: (Public, error) An error indicating that the provided username is invalid (e.g., empty).\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Usecase Pattern**: Encapsulates the core business rules for user management, acting as an intermediary between HTTP handlers and the `UserRepository`.\n    - **Username Management**: Implements logic for ensuring unique usernames, handling conflicts (e.g., appending random numbers), and managing cooldown periods for released usernames.\n    - **Activity Tracking**: Utilizes `LastActive` timestamps to determine user presence and identify inactive users for cleanup.\n    - **Error Handling**: Defines specific, descriptive errors for various business rule violations.",
  "pkg/utils/idgen.go": "- **File Path**: `pkg/utils/idgen.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides a utility function for generating universally unique identifiers (UUIDs).\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `GenerateID()`: (Public) Returns a new unique identifier string using the `github.com/google/uuid` library.\n",
  "public/css/style.css": "- **File Path**: `public/css/style.css`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides custom CSS styles for the frontend application, including utility classes for transitions and specific styling for a custom scrollbar in the user list.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **CSS Rules**:\n        - `.hidden`: Sets `display: none;` for elements that should be hidden, often used with JavaScript for toggling visibility.\n        - `.modal-overlay`: Applies a `transition` property for smooth opacity changes.\n        - `.user-list-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar`: Styles the width of the scrollbar for Webkit browsers.\n        - `.user-list-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-track`: Styles the background of the scrollbar track.\n        - `.user-list-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb`: Styles the scrollable thumb of the scrollbar, including its background color and border-radius.\n        - `.user-list-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover`: Styles the scrollbar thumb on hover.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Custom UI styling for specific components (e.g., scrollbars).\n    - Utility classes for common UI states (e.g., `hidden`).\n",
  "public/index.html": "- **File Path**: `public/index.html`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Serves as the main entry point and structural blueprint for the client-side SSE chat application. It defines the overall layout, includes necessary CSS and JavaScript resources, and provides placeholders for dynamic content like user lists, chat messages, and a username input modal.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **HTML Structure / Elements**:\n        - `\u003cdiv id=\"app\"\u003e`: (Main container) The primary application interface, initially hidden, which will be shown after a user joins.\n            - `\u003caside\u003e`: (Sidebar) Contains the active user list and current user panel.\n                - `\u003cdiv id=\"user-list\"\u003e`: Placeholder for the dynamically rendered list of active users.\n                - `\u003cdiv id=\"current-user-panel\"\u003e`: Placeholder for the current user's information and actions.\n            - `\u003cmain\u003e`: (Main chat area) Contains the chat header, message list, and message input form.\n                - `\u003cheader id=\"chat-header\"\u003e`: Displays the selected chat partner's username.\n                    - `\u003ch2 id=\"chat-header-username\"\u003e`: Displays the name of the user currently being chatted with.\n                    - `\u003cinput id=\"message-search-input\"\u003e`: (Hidden) Input for searching messages.\n                - `\u003cdiv id=\"message-list\"\u003e`: Container for chat messages, designed to scroll to the bottom.\n                    - `\u003cbutton id=\"load-more-messages\"\u003e`: (Hidden) Button to load older messages.\n                - `\u003cfooter\u003e`: Contains the typing indicator and message input form.\n                    - `\u003cdiv id=\"typing-indicator\"\u003e`: Displays who is currently typing.\n                    - `\u003cform id=\"message-form\"\u003e`: Form for sending messages.\n                        - `\u003cinput id=\"message-input\"\u003e`: Text input for composing messages (initially disabled).\n                        - `\u003cbutton id=\"send-button\"\u003e`: Button to send messages (initially disabled).\n        - `\u003cdiv id=\"username-modal\"\u003e`: (Modal) An overlay for users to enter their username before joining the chat.\n            - `\u003cform id=\"join-form\"\u003e`: Form for submitting the desired username.\n                - `\u003cinput id=\"username-input\"\u003e`: Input field for the username.\n                - `\u003cp id=\"modal-error\"\u003e`: Displays error messages related to username submission.\n                - `\u003cbutton id=\"join-button\"\u003e`: Button to submit the username and join the chat.\n        - `\u003caudio id=\"notification-sound\"\u003e`: An audio element with a base64 encoded sound, likely for notifications.\n    - **External Resources**:\n        - `https://cdn.tailwindcss.com`: Link to the Tailwind CSS CDN for utility-first styling.\n        - `/css/style.css`: Link to custom CSS styles.\n        - `/js/lib/dexie.min.js`: Script inclusion for the Dexie.js library (IndexedDB wrapper).\n        - `/js/main.js`: The main application JavaScript logic.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Single Page Application (SPA) Structure**: The main application content (`#app`) is initially hidden, indicating that JavaScript (`main.js`) will manage its visibility and dynamic content loading.\n    - **Modal-First Interaction**: The `username-modal` is displayed by default, requiring user input before the main chat interface is accessible.\n    - **Semantic HTML with IDs**: Extensive use of `id` attributes on key elements, facilitating easy selection and manipulation by JavaScript.\n    - **Third-Party Libraries**: Integrates Tailwind CSS for styling and Dexie.js for client-side database interactions.\n    - **Inline Resources**: Includes a base64 encoded audio file directly in the HTML for a notification sound.",
  "public/js/api.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/api.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides a client-side interface for interacting with the backend API endpoints, abstracting away the `fetch` API details and handling common request/response patterns.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `API_BASE`: (Private, string) The base path for all API endpoints (`/api`).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `request(endpoint: string, options: object)`: (Private, async) A generic helper function for making HTTP requests. It sets default headers (JSON), handles `fetch` calls, checks for `response.ok`, parses JSON responses, and throws an `Error` if the response is not successful. It returns `null` for 204/202 status codes.\n        - `join(desiredUsername: string): Promise\u003c{userId: string, username: string, activeUsers: User[]}\u003e`: (Public, async) Sends a POST request to `/api/join` to register a new user.\n        - `changeUsername(userId: string, newUsername: string): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e`: (Public, async) Sends a POST request to `/api/change-username` to update a user's username.\n        - `sendMessage(fromUserId: string, toUserId: string, text: string): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e`: (Public, async) Sends a POST request to `/api/message` to send a chat message.\n        - `sendTyping(userId: string, toUserId: string, typing: boolean): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e`: (Public, async) Sends a POST request to `/api/typing` to broadcast a user's typing status.\n        - `getSnapshot(userId: string, lastEventId: string): Promise\u003c{events: any[], activeUsers: User[], lastEventId: string}\u003e`: (Public, async) Sends a GET request to `/api/snapshot` to retrieve initial events and active users, optionally specifying a `lastEventId` for event catch-up.\n    - **Types**:\n        - `User`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **API Client**: Encapsulates all communication with the backend, providing a clean interface for other frontend modules.\n    - **Error Handling**: Centralized error handling for API responses, parsing error messages from the backend.\n    - **JSON Communication**: Assumes and enforces JSON for request and response bodies.\n",
  "public/js/components/avatar.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/components/avatar.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides utility functions for generating unique colors from strings and creating user avatar HTML elements for the frontend.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `simpleHash(str: string): number`: (Private) A basic string hashing function that converts a string into a 32-bit integer hash.\n        - `stringToColor(str: string): string`: (Private) Generates an HSL color string based on the hash of the input string, used for avatar background colors.\n        - `createAvatar(user: User, extraClasses: string = ''): HTMLElement`: (Public) Creates a `div` HTML element representing a user's avatar. It displays the first letter of the username, sets a background color derived from the `userId`, and applies specified CSS classes.\n    - **Types**:\n        - `User`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`, representing a user object.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Frontend component utility for visual representation of users.\n    - Deterministic color generation based on user ID for consistent avatars.\n",
  "public/js/lib/dexie.min.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/lib/dexie.min.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: This file serves as a placeholder for the Dexie.js library, which is intended for managing client-side IndexedDB interactions.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - No definitions are present in this placeholder file.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Third-party library inclusion (placeholder).\n",
  "public/js/main.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/main.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: The main client-side application logic. It orchestrates user interactions, API calls, SSE event processing, and UI updates to manage the chat session.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `state`: (Private, object) Manages the application's current state, including `currentUser`, `activeUsers` (a Map), `selectedUserId`, and `typingTimeout` for debouncing.\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `handleChangeUsername()`: (Private, async) Prompts for a new username, calls the API to change it, optimistically updates the UI, and saves the change locally.\n        - `handleUserClick(user: User)`: (Private, async) Sets the selected chat partner, updates UI elements, hides typing indicators, and loads/renders historical messages for the conversation.\n        - `updateUserList(users: User[])`: (Private) Updates the internal `activeUsers` map and triggers a re-render of the user list UI.\n        - `processEvent(event: object)`: (Private) A central handler for incoming SSE events (e.g., user joined/left, message, typing status). It updates the application state, persists data to the local store, and triggers relevant UI updates.\n        - `startChatSession()`: (Private, async) Initializes the chat session by fetching the last known event ID, retrieving a snapshot of events and active users from the API, processing these initial events, and then connecting to the SSE stream to listen for real-time updates.\n        - `handleSendMessage(e: Event)`: (Private, async) Handles sending a chat message. It prevents default form submission, calls the API to send the message, clears the input, and stops any active typing indicators.\n        - `handleTyping()`: (Private) Manages sending typing start/stop events to the server, implementing debouncing to avoid excessive API calls.\n        - `handleJoin(e: Event)`: (Private, async) Handles the user joining the chat. It validates the username, calls the API to join, saves the current user, updates the UI (hides modal, shows app), attaches event listeners for chat interactions, and then initiates the chat session.\n        - `init()`: (Private, async) The application's entry point, executed on `DOMContentLoaded`. It initializes the local data store, clears any previous user session, displays the join modal, and sets up the join form listener.\n    - **Types**:\n        - `User`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`.\n        - `Message`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Event-Driven Architecture**: Reacts to user interactions and server-sent events.\n    - **State Management**: Uses a simple `state` object to manage application data.\n    - **Dependency Injection (Implicit)**: Imports and uses `api`, `store`, `ui`, and `sseClient` modules.\n    - **Asynchronous Operations**: Heavily uses `async/await` for API calls and IndexedDB operations.\n    - **Debouncing**: Implements debouncing for the typing indicator.\n    - **UI/Logic Separation**: Delegates UI rendering to the `ui` module and data persistence to the `store` module.\n",
  "public/js/sse.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/sse.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Manages the client-side Server-Sent Events (SSE) connection, handling connection establishment, event reception, automatic reconnection logic, and dispatching events to registered listeners. It also persists received events and the last event ID to the local store.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `RECONNECT_DELAY_MS`: (Private, array of numbers) Defines the exponential backoff delays for reconnection attempts.\n        - `eventSource`: (Private, `EventSource | null`) The active `EventSource` instance.\n        - `reconnectAttempt`: (Private, number) Counter for reconnection attempts.\n        - `currentUserId`: (Private, string) Stores the ID of the current user for reconnection purposes.\n        - `listeners`: (Private, `Map\u003cstring, Function[]\u003e`) A map to store event type to handler function mappings.\n        - `sseClient`: (Public, object) The exported object containing methods to interact with the SSE client.\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `dispatch(event: Event)`: (Private) Processes an incoming SSE event. It parses the event data, normalizes it, persists it to `store.addEvent` and `store.saveLastEventId`, and then dispatches the normalized event to all registered handlers for that event type.\n        - `connectInternal(userId: string, lastEventId: string)`: (Private) Establishes or re-establishes the `EventSource` connection. It constructs the SSE URL with `userId` and `lastEventId`, sets up `onopen` and `onerror` handlers (including reconnection logic with exponential backoff), and registers `dispatch` for various SSE event types (message, user_joined, etc.) and a special handler for `heartbeat`.\n        - `sseClient.connect(userId: string, lastEventId: string)`: (Public method) Initializes the SSE connection for a given user, starting from a specified `lastEventId`.\n        - `sseClient.close()`: (Public method) Closes the active SSE connection.\n        - `sseClient.addEventListener(type: string, handler: Function)`: (Public method) Registers a handler function to be called when a specific SSE event `type` is received.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Server-Sent Events (SSE)**: Utilizes the browser's native `EventSource` API for real-time, unidirectional communication.\n    - **Automatic Reconnection**: Implements exponential backoff for reconnection attempts in case of connection errors.\n    - **Event Dispatcher**: Provides a simple publish-subscribe mechanism for other modules to listen to specific SSE event types.\n    - **Event Persistence**: Automatically saves all received events and the `lastEventId` to the local `store` for session continuity and catch-up.\n    - **Heartbeat Handling**: Specifically handles `heartbeat` events to update the `lastEventId` without triggering other UI logic.\n",
  "public/js/store.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/store.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides client-side data persistence using IndexedDB (via Dexie.js) and `localStorage`. It manages the current user's session, stores chat messages, and keeps track of the last processed event ID for SSE.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `DB_NAME`: (Private, string) The name of the IndexedDB database.\n        - `SESSION_USER_ID_KEY`: (Private, string) `localStorage` key for the current user's ID.\n        - `SESSION_USERNAME_KEY`: (Private, string) `localStorage` key for the current user's username.\n        - `LAST_EVENT_ID_KEY`: (Private, string) `kvstore` key for the last processed event ID.\n        - `db`: (Private, `Dexie`) The Dexie.js database instance.\n        - `store`: (Public, object) The exported object containing methods for data storage and retrieval.\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `store.init()`: (Public, async) Initializes the Dexie.js database, defining its version and object stores (`messages`, `events`, `kvstore`).\n        - `store.saveCurrentUser(user: User)`: (Public, async) Saves the current user's `userId` and `username` to `localStorage`.\n        - `store.getCurrentUser(): Promise\u003cUser | null\u003e`: (Public, async) Retrieves the current user's `userId` and `username` from `localStorage` and reconstructs a `User` object.\n        - `store.clearCurrentUser()`: (Public, async) Removes the current user's data from `localStorage` and deletes/reopens the IndexedDB database, effectively clearing all local chat data.\n        - `store.getLastEventId(): Promise\u003cstring | null\u003e`: (Public, async) Retrieves the `lastEventId` from the `kvstore` in IndexedDB. Defaults to '0' if not found.\n        - `store.saveLastEventId(eventId: string)`: (Public, async) Saves the given `eventId` to the `kvstore` in IndexedDB.\n        - `store.addEvent(event: any)`: (Public, async) Adds a generic event to the `events` object store in IndexedDB. Handles `ConstraintError` (duplicate eventId) gracefully.\n        - `store.addMessage(message: Message)`: (Public, async) Adds a chat message to the `messages` object store in IndexedDB. It generates a `conversationId` for easy retrieval of messages between two users. Handles `ConstraintError` gracefully.\n        - `store.getMessages(userId1: string, userId2: string, page: number, pageSize: number): Promise\u003cMessage[]\u003e`: (Public, async) Retrieves a paginated list of messages between two specified users from IndexedDB, sorted by timestamp.\n    - **Types**:\n        - `User`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`.\n        - `Message`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **Local Storage**: Uses `localStorage` for lightweight session data (current user).\n    - **IndexedDB (via Dexie.js)**: Utilizes IndexedDB for more structured and persistent storage of chat messages and events, crucial for offline capabilities and event catch-up.\n    - **Data Schema**: Defines clear schemas for `messages`, `events`, and `kvstore` in IndexedDB.\n    - **Conversation ID**: Generates a consistent `conversationId` by sorting user IDs to easily query messages between any two users.\n    - **Error Handling**: Catches `ConstraintError` for duplicate entries, preventing application crashes for idempotent operations.",
  "public/js/types.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/types.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines JSDoc `@typedef` types for core data structures (`User`, `Message`) used across the frontend JavaScript application, enhancing code readability and enabling type checking.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `User`: (JSDoc typedef object) Represents a user in the chat system.\n            - Properties: `userId` (string), `username` (string), `isOnline` (boolean).\n        - `Message`: (JSDoc typedef object) Represents a chat message.\n            - Properties: `eventId` (string), `fromUserId` (string), `toUserId` (string), `text` (string), `timestamp` (string, ISO Date format).\n",
  "public/js/ui.js": "- **File Path**: `public/js/ui.js`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Manages all user interface interactions and rendering for the chat application. It provides functions to display/hide elements, render user lists, chat windows, messages, and typing indicators.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `ui`: (Public, object) An exported object containing references to various DOM elements and methods for UI manipulation.\n            - Fields: `appContainer`, `modal`, `modalError`, `userList`, `currentUserPanel`, `messageList`, `messageInput`, `sendButton`, `chatHeader`, `typingIndicator` (all HTMLElement references).\n    - **Functions / Methods**: (All are methods of the `ui` object)\n        - `showModal()`: (Public) Displays the username modal by removing the 'hidden' CSS class.\n        - `hideModal()`: (Public) Hides the username modal by adding the 'hidden' CSS class.\n        - `displayError(message: string)`: (Public) Sets the text content of the modal error display.\n        - `showApp()`: (Public) Displays the main application container by removing the 'hidden' CSS class.\n        - `renderUsers(users: User[], currentUserId: string, selectedUserId: string | null)`: (Public) Renders the list of active users in the sidebar, sorting them alphabetically, filtering out the current user, and highlighting the selected user.\n        - `renderCurrentUserPanel(user: User, onChangeUsername: () =\u003e void)`: (Public) Renders the current user's avatar and username in a dedicated panel, including a \"Change\" button with a click handler.\n        - `renderChatWindow(contactUser: User)`: (Public) Configures the chat header and message input area based on the selected contact user, enabling/disabling message input and send button.\n        - `addMessage(message: Message, isOwnMessage: boolean, fromUser: User)`: (Public) Appends a new message bubble to the message list, styling it based on whether it's an outgoing or incoming message, and scrolls to the bottom.\n        - `showTypingIndicator(user: User)`: (Public) Displays a typing indicator showing which user is typing.\n        - `hideTypingIndicator()`: (Public) Hides the typing indicator.\n    - **Types**:\n        - `User`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`.\n        - `Message`: (JSDoc typedef) Imported from `../types.js`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - **DOM Manipulation**: Directly interacts with the DOM to render and update the user interface.\n    - **Component-like Structure**: The `ui` object encapsulates all UI-related logic, acting as a single point of interaction for the main application logic.\n    - **CSS Utility Classes**: Leverages Tailwind CSS utility classes for styling.\n"
